// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INPUTS — Regime Engine
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

i_reqMaConfirm = input.bool(true, "Trend Requires MA Confirmation", group="Regime Engine", tooltip="THE CONSOLIDATION PRIOR: a breakout alone is NOT a trend. At least N of the active HTF MAs must agree with the breakout direction, otherwise the regime stays classified as a range. This encodes 'assume the market consolidates 80% of the time'.")
i_maConfirmMin = input.int(4, "MAs Required to Confirm Trend", minval=1, maxval=6, group="Regime Engine", tooltip="How many active EMAs must agree with a breakout (correct side + correct slope) before it is classified as a trend rather than a range. Automatically clamped to the number of ACTIVE EMAs. v1.8: with ZERO active EMAs the confirmation now FAILS instead of vacuously passing (v1.7's 0 >= 0 test inverted the consolidation prior and made every breakout a confirmed trend).")

